at makes each one feel  unique right so the Ranger is kind of  your your well balanced in class right  it's it's a little bit nimble it packs a  good punch and allows you to go out and  do some some really good exploration  it's very mobile it's got that jetpack  you've seen a little on so that's kind  of like the beginner class like when I  first jump into the game that'll  probably a good one to start off  absolutely absolutely the Colossus is a  little heavier you're sacrificing some  nimbleness for more armor it's got that  cool shield that comes up instead of a  dodge so you're really there to draw a  fire and to protect your squadmates  but depending on how you load it out  it's up to you right you're not locked  into a class of defender you can go out  and kind of approach that in the way  that you want to approach it the storm  is a much more mystical suit you can  think of the the power source in these  suits as you can either use it to power  gadgets and devices or you can use it to  project power externally so you notice  on the storm suit it's got these cool  seals on one arm and that allows it to  project elemental power and gives it  these great attacks and then it is  tapping into  more mysterious power of the world is  that still something that you're  grounding in in a science or do you want  it to feel very mystical and mysterious  so you wanted to feel mysterious this is  the cool thing about a science fantasy  property we don't have to explain all of  the technology that goes behind it you  can kind of give the general sense hey  these are these javelins suits they run  in this cool power source and and of  course being a part of the the EA  background  I know microtransactions loot boxes are  you know they're a big part of the  conversations but it doesn't sound like  that's gonna be a big part of what  anthem is about no it's not and in fact  from when we very first started  designing anthem back in 2013 2012 we  were really thinking of an expe